{"id": "EUVD-2026-93096", "enisaUuid": "e1782a58-89e8-3948-8770-4a4f1ae093e3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix reparse buffer bounds in cifs_query_reparse_point()\n\nIn cifs_query_reparse_point(), the start >= end check before casting to\nstruct reparse_data_buffer * only ensures the start pointer is within the\nresponse. It fails to verify that there is enough space remaining for the\nfixed 8-byte header of the structure.\n\nIf a server provides a DataOffset that leaves less than 8 bytes remaining,\nthe check passes, but subsequent reads of ReparseTag and ReparseDataLength\nwill occur out-of-bounds.\n\nFix this by ensuring the remaining space is at least the size of the\nreparse_data_buffer structure before accessing its fields.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa00eead258e4fe8158a3a3e2d65facf06274abd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d67f155fe5813cfb02a551a9a12d6ea06a902e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1152c96a3002e3df6b9a5b007cecaa7b19b4f79", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8dc5db3a0e583ea8d31d0613cefd99e93e095c3c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5f0306e731e2f46e91419eae57eee3a241c055e0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98168", "GHSA-p97w-7qmq-228w"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07e7d777-346f-398f-8cab-c436ba2eecf9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "0a5077ac-b791-33d4-bfef-5e3c65464816", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "56e84c64fc257a95728ee73165456b025c48d408 <8dc5db3a0e583ea8d31d0613cefd99e93e095c3c"}, {"id": "0bb2cda0-fde1-39bb-ac27-242ea3fc0d7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "848d78e3625f15de09d34a562dc49a98b78a62f3 <aa00eead258e4fe8158a3a3e2d65facf06274abd"}, {"id": "0c9b0515-7edf-325b-8e63-506c5f131d6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.94 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "1624e570-5a2f-3641-8ad0-438e58e5d0fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "56e84c64fc257a95728ee73165456b025c48d408 <5f0306e731e2f46e91419eae57eee3a241c055e0"}, {"id": "3235f196-bd22-34cb-9b9c-ac921fda65bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15.3 <6.16"}, {"id": "35da32f1-91f8-3d6a-ac86-ebdc708c9dcf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "488dc9fa-13ed-30e6-8ebc-e070ce54333e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "52c357cb-26bd-3163-bf9b-a7d690ade940", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "928ddd36-387c-3e63-b9ab-08b6a0266a82", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c13b779d26b3702fba8f7d5fe757aba5bda85fd0"}, {"id": "a4d33475-6227-36b1-8f54-c7be8a81e6c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "56e84c64fc257a95728ee73165456b025c48d408 <d1152c96a3002e3df6b9a5b007cecaa7b19b4f79"}, {"id": "ac96c812-9d82-3065-8a79-0ded9c76370b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "befe7e5f-c3dd-3e4d-8ca2-94abc858015e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "48ca7139ab7f0bbed95ff7a901ea497017769657 <3d67f155fe5813cfb02a551a9a12d6ea06a902e9"}, {"id": "cb2339b3-85d0-37a7-82d9-be1edd2cf555", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d3b11940-925f-39ea-97a9-c39b9748dffa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "dcd5aef5-6a06-3f08-a7f6-9a733cf3f7a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor